# iOS workflow

**Scope:** Binding only when `dev-ios-scope.mdc` marks this workspace active (iOS). When inactive, ignore this entire rule.

This rule ships with the `dev-ios` Cursor plugin. Do not copy skills, rules, MCP, or hooks into `.cursor/` or `~/.cursor`.

The open workspace is the app you build and test. Follow **How to build or test this app** in `skills/build-ios-apps/references/session-defaults.md` (that app’s yaml, then one MCP call). Do not build the plugin repo, do not stage plugin files, and do not probe `session_*`.

## MCP servers

Xcode and Simulator execution is MCP-only (`xcode-mcp-only.mdc`). Cursor native file tools (Read, Write, Grep, Glob) are the project source surface.

- **XcodeBuildMCP** — `build_sim` and `test_sim` only. See **Simulator UI forbidden** below.

Before **every** `build_sim` or `test_sim`, follow `skills/build-ios-apps/references/session-defaults.md`: read this host’s `.xcodebuildmcp/config.yaml` and pass **explicit** `projectPath`, `scheme`, `configuration`, `simulatorId`, and `derivedDataPath` on every build tool call (do not use `session_*` tools). Unit tests: `build_sim` with `buildForTesting: true` plus the full `tests` profile (including `testProductsPath`), then `test_sim` with the `testProductsPath` that file chooses and `simulatorId` only (do not use source-mode). Use `simulator-status.sh status` when you need inventory. Status scripts **never** terminate `xcodebuild` (killing mid-run corrupts simulator databases and SPM `SourcePackages`). After verification run `simulator-shutdown.sh shutdown` or `shutdown-all` only when `xcodebuild_count=0`. On chat `sessionEnd` or **Stop**, `hooks/agent-session-lifecycle.sh` only closes registry rows and does not send signals. In-flight **XcodeBuildMCP** `build_sim` / `test_sim` / `clean` calls are recorded per `conversation_id` for diagnostics only; **hooks do not send signals to `xcodebuild`** (Stop/sessionEnd must not touch Xcode or other agents' builds). After the user presses **Stop** during `build_sim`, wait for the prior MCP run to finish or let the user recover manually. Do not start another `build_sim`, do not MCP `clean`, and do not delete `SourcePackages` until the previous one has completed or been aborted by Cursor/XcodeBuildMCP. Profiles:
- `app` → `build_sim` with all fields from yaml profile `app` in **tool_input** every time ([checkout-environment.md](skills/build-ios-apps/references/checkout-environment.md))
- `tests` → `build_sim` (`buildForTesting: true` with full yaml `tests` profile in tool args) then `test_sim` (`testProductsPath` from [session-defaults.md](skills/build-ios-apps/references/session-defaults.md) + simulator from yaml)

Yaml location, bootstrap, and argument lists: `skills/build-ios-apps/references/session-defaults.md`. One device only (configured UDID from yaml). Do not hardcode a device name or iOS version. Do not call `boot_sim`, `open_sim`, or `build_run_sim`. Never run `simctl clone`, boot a second simulator, or leave parallel-test clone devices (`Clone N of …`) running. Clones appear in `simulator-status.sh status`; shut them down with `simulator-shutdown.sh` when `xcodebuild_count=0`.

## After every code change

Anyone (human or agent) who edits Swift, Objective-C, Xcode project files, or other compile-affecting host/extension sources **must** verify before calling the work done, opening a PR, or moving to an unrelated task.

| Step | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| Compile | Run **`build_sim`** via **XcodeBuildMCP** after reading [session-defaults.md](skills/build-ios-apps/references/session-defaults.md) and [checkout-environment.md](skills/build-ios-apps/references/checkout-environment.md) (full yaml profile in **tool_input** every build call). Never claim verification from Shell `xcodebuild`. Fix all **new** compile errors only after a successful build. |
| Lint | Clear new warnings surfaced by **`build_sim`** and Cursor diagnostics in touched files. Do not leave new warnings in modified code. |
| Done | **Must not** claim success without a fresh build result from this session. Answering a follow-up question does not replace a build after prior edits. |

If the build fails, fix the cause and rebuild. Do not hand off a broken tree.

Host projects may document scheme names and test scope in `docs/testing.md` or `docs/development.md`; the **obligation to build** lives here in the plugin, not in host docs.

## Simulator UI forbidden

Never open Simulator.app and never launch an app in the Simulator. Allowed XcodeBuildMCP tools are `build_sim` and `test_sim` only. `test_sim` runs unit tests with mocks. Do not call `boot_sim`, `open_sim`, `build_run_sim`, `install_app_sim`, `launch_app_sim`, `stop_app_sim`, `screenshot`, `snapshot_ui`, `tap`, `touch`, `long_press`, `swipe`, `drag`, `gesture`, `button`, `key_press`, `key_sequence`, `type_text`, `wait_for_ui`, `record_sim_video`, or `debug_attach_sim`. Do not run `serve-sim`, `swiftui-preview-browser.py`, `open -a Simulator`, `simctl boot`, or `simctl launch`. If a task needs the Simulator window, stop and say this plugin does not launch Simulator UI.

## Bundled skill scripts

Scripts under `plugins/dev-ios/skills/**/scripts/` are allowed when a loaded skill instructs you to run them. Do not write new orchestration scripts outside that tree. Run from the host project checkout.

| Script | Skill | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `skills/build-ios-apps/scripts/resolve-derived-data-path.sh` | `build-ios-apps` | Resolve/sync Xcode DerivedData into yaml (`--sync-config`) for this repo only |
| `skills/build-ios-apps/scripts/bootstrap-xcodebuildmcp-config.sh` | `build-ios-apps` | Create `.xcodebuildmcp/config.yaml` from scratch when MCP cannot start |
| `skills/build-ios-apps/scripts/xcodebuildmcp-with-xcode-derived-data.sh` | `build-ios-apps` | MCP launcher (`mcp.json`); pinned XcodeBuildMCP npm (no startup host bind) |
| `skills/ios-simulator-browser/scripts/simulator-status.sh` | `ios-simulator-browser` | Simulator inventory and `xcodebuild` load signals; `status` only |
| `skills/ios-simulator-browser/scripts/simulator-shutdown.sh` | `ios-simulator-browser` | `simctl shutdown` of booted devices; no signals, no Simulator.app quit |
| `skills/ios-ettrace-performance/scripts/*` | `ios-ettrace-performance` | ETTrace capture (see skill) |
| `skills/ios-memgraph-leaks/scripts/*` | `ios-memgraph-leaks` | Memgraph summarize (see skill) |

Do not use MCP `list_sims` text alone to decide whether simulators are off. Use `ios-simulator-browser` → `simulator-status.sh status`.

Never terminate `xcodebuild`, never `kill` PIDs from `status`, never delete `SourcePackages`. The plugin does not send signals, does not call `simctl terminate`, and does not quit Simulator.app; `simctl shutdown` only through `simulator-shutdown.sh`. Use `simulator-shutdown.sh` after verification when the host policy requires it and `xcodebuild_count` is 0.

## Host test-specific rules

Default unit-test procedure and decision logic belong in the host project's testing policy (`docs/testing.md` or equivalent). **Concrete** per-scope overrides belong in a separate host file (suggested: `docs/testing-specific-rules-by-classes.md`).

When `test_sim` fails repeatedly for the same scope, read `build-ios-apps` → `references/test-specific-rules.md` for how to create that file, what to put in each row, and the living-document rule (update the host file before reporting verification done).

## Pairing skills

- `ios-debugger-agent` pairs with `ios-simulator-browser` for simulator status and shutdown before and after build or test.
- `ios-ettrace-performance` and `ios-memgraph-leaks` pair with `ios-debugger-agent` for `build_sim` and `test_sim` only.
